But the moment I got there, I felt my blood turn to ice.%K%P
我全身的血液，一下子凝固住了。%K%P
In contrast to the properly reinforced front door, I found\nMitoko's room in a state of serious disarray.%K%P
和紧闭的玄关形成对照的，\n是窗户玻璃凄惨地散落一地的美都子的房间。%K%P
The window was smashed, with broken glass littering the\nfloor, and Mitoko herself was nowhere to be seen.%K%P
我冲进的这间屋子已经是乱七八糟，\n更糟糕的是她的身影并没有出现。%K%P
At that realization, I immediately rushed out to the\ncorridor and started checking all the rooms in the house,\none by one.%K%P
冲到走廊，依次打开手边的门，\n一片又一片的空荡荡让我的失望愈发强烈。%K%P
